data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch_dev_1.md\", \"content\": \"This is your first dispatch for campaign csrocfw. Implement exactly this, in your own clone of the `subject` repository, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. Create `src/greet.py` containing a function `greet(name)` that returns the\\n   string `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (i.e. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. Create `tests/test_greet.py` with unit tests covering:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\n3. Run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` yourself and confirm it exits 0\\n   (all tests pass). Fix anything that fails before replying.\\n\\n4. Commit your work to your own branch.\\n\\n5. Reply with a summary of what you did, including the exact command you ran\\n   to verify the tests pass and its result.\\n\\nDo not implement anything beyond this — just the function and its tests.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

